# Caddy in front of the edu-suite dashboard.
#
# `local_certs` makes Caddy issue certificates from its own internal CA (no public
# ACME), which is the right choice for a home/LAN box. The dashboard is served at
# the site address below and reverse-proxied to the dashboard container.
#
# Access from THIS machine:  https://edu.localhost  (localhost is auto-trusted).
# Access from OTHER LAN devices: change the site address to this machine's name or
# IP (e.g. `edu.mybox.lan` or `https://192.168.1.50`) and import Caddy's root CA on
# those devices (see deploy/README.md). For quick, trust-free testing, change the
# site address to `http://edu.localhost` (plain HTTP, no cert).

{
	local_certs
}

edu.localhost {
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy dashboard:8800
}
